---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { STATS, LOGOS } from '../consts';
const marquee = [...LOGOS, ...LOGOS];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Teleforce — Bilingual LATAM BPO | Teleforce"
  description="Teleforce is a bilingual LATAM BPO for U.S. companies, built on a Fortune 500-grade support backbone, 30+ years deep. The story behind the infrastructure."
>
  <header class="ahead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cat">About</div>
      <h1>An established backbone, pointed at U.S. companies.</h1>
      <div class="ameta"><span>Bilingual LATAM BPO</span><span>30+ years operating</span></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="post">
    <p class="lead">Teleforce is a bilingual, LATAM-based BPO for U.S. companies. What makes it different isn't a pitch deck — it's what sits underneath it: a Fortune 500-grade support backbone that has served global enterprises for more than three decades.</p>

    <p>Most LATAM BPO and staffing vendors are startups. They're building their recruiting pipeline, their QA process, their security posture, and their training program at the same time they're building your team. You feel that ramp — in the first ninety days especially, when the org is still learning how to run itself.</p>

    <p>Teleforce skips that. The infrastructure already exists.</p>

    <h2>An established backbone</h2>
    <p>Behind Teleforce is a Fortune 500-grade support network — 30+ years operating, across 20+ industries, with recruiting, training, quality assurance, information security, and uptime processes that already meet the standards of large global enterprises. Teleforce is the channel that brings that backbone to growing U.S. companies as dedicated, fully English/Spanish bilingual teams.</p>
    <p>When you engage Teleforce, you're not waiting for a young vendor to figure out operations. You inherit a system that's been refined across decades and across some of the most demanding accounts in the world.</p>

    <div class="trust" style="border-radius:14px;margin:30px 0">
      <div class="row">
        {STATS.map((s) => (
          <div class="stat"><span class="n">{s.n}</span><span class="k">{s.k}</span></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Trusted by global enterprises</h2>
    <p>You'll see names like UPS, American Express, SAP, and Nike associated with the network behind Teleforce. They're enterprises that backbone has supported over 30+ years — proof of the reach and the standard it operates to. It's how a growing company gets enterprise-grade operations without enterprise scale.</p>

    <div class="logos" style="border-radius:14px;margin:24px 0;padding-top:24px">
      <div class="lab">Trusted by global enterprises for 30+ years</div>
      <div class="marquee-mask">
        <div class="marquee">
          {marquee.map((name) => <span>{name}</span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Why bilingual, why LATAM</h2>
    <p>The U.S. market is bilingual, and serving it well means English and Spanish at the same standard, on the same hours, from the same team. Latin America is one of the few talent pools where native-level Spanish and strong English coexist at scale — on U.S. business hours, with clear, accent-neutral Spanish and higher agent retention than offshore alternatives. That's the model: dedicated agents who work as an extension of your brand, with same-day feedback loops instead of overnight handoffs.</p>

    <h2>Two ways to engage</h2>
    <p>You can hire the talent and run it yourself, or hand us the whole operation. <strong>Recruitment</strong> — we source, screen, and interview qualified LATAM agents; you interview, hire, and manage them, with a 60–90 day replacement guarantee. <strong>Managed BPO</strong> — a full-time-equivalent seat where we handle salary, payroll, HR, recruiting, facilities, and IT. Pricing is quote-based, by role and volume.</p>

    <h2>More than support: collections</h2>
    <p>Most clients start with customer support, but the same bilingual team is built to do something most support shops can't: recover revenue. Teleforce runs <strong>first-party, pre-delinquent and early-stage collections</strong> — friendly, on-brand outreach in the early delinquency buckets where recovery rates are highest and tone matters most. Because we collect in your name as an extension of your brand, the customer relationship stays yours. And native Spanish outreach reaches Hispanic accounts an English-only team simply can't — lifting recovery without adding risk. First-party collections supports flexible pricing — by hire, by seat, or per program.</p>

    <h2>A rare layer: U.S. legal oversight</h2>
    <p>Teleforce operates with U.S. legal and compliance oversight of data handling and consumer-contact practices — supervision that's uncommon in this category. For companies in regulated or contact-sensitive industries, that's not a nice-to-have; it's the difference between a vendor and a partner you can stand behind.</p>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h4>Let's scope your team.</h4>
      <p>Tell us your channels, languages, and rough monthly volume. We'll come back with a staffing plan and a go-live date — usually within two business days.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="btn btn-amber">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
